<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - NationsBank downgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - NationsBank downgraded.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brown Brothers Harriman said analyst Nancy Bush lowered her near-term rating on NationsBank Corp to market perform from outperform.</p>
<p>-- Cited stock valuation and risk related to Montgomery Securities acquisition.</p>
<p>-- In a research note, Bush said deal was &quot;absolutely ill-advised and will add an additional element of risk and volatility to the NationsBank earnings stream.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Referred to investment bank acquisitions as &quot;an unfortunate trend,&quot; in part because of incompatibility of regional bank and investment bank cultures.</p>
<p>-- Said stock had reached valuation target of $60 per share in price and 70 percent relative-valuation to S&amp;P 500.</p>
<p>-- Kept long-term rating at hold.</p>
<p>-- Shares fell 1/4 to 65.</p>
</text>
